Along $XC$, move $1$ square up. A copy of $\mathbf{a}$ moves $1$ square up. Thus $XC=1|\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{XC}=\mathbf{a}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c}&=\overrightarrow{OX}+\overrightarrow{XC}\\&=-3\mathbf{b}+\mathbf{a}\\&=\mathbf{a}-3\mathbf{b}
\end{aligned}
